  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZAIDAL WOMEN AND GIRLS INITIATIVE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to reach 200 women and girls to empower them with skills and furnish them with productive skills to help avoid negative livelihood coping strategies. Beneficiaries will be selected through a community-based targeting and selection process. Training will be provide in useful skills such as tailoring and knitting, hair dressing, grinding and pasta making, and soap and antiseptic production, and assistance will be provided to pass on these skills and to sell products produced. These skills will help improve livelihoods and strengthen the resilience of women and girls to poverty and extremist influence, and develop their responses to emergency threats and vulnerabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
